From: Xun2202 <xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 07:06:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] android: play a silent audio loop while web-source caches
 download
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

On HarmonyOS 卓易通 the app process is suspended within seconds of
leaving the foreground even with a dataSync foreground service, a partial
wake lock and a battery-optimisation exemption (6.2.0-harmony.5 log:
last progress 14:55:44, requests thawed and timed out at 14:58:51 when
the user reopened the app). Audio output is what the host keeps running,
so HttpCacheService becomes a mediaPlayback service and loops a silent
MODE_STATIC AudioTrack for its lifetime. No audio focus is requested, so
other apps' playback is unaffected; the loop is driven by the audio HAL
and costs no CPU. The environment (Build fields, cgroup) is logged once
per start to tell compatibility layers apart in bug reports.

Also dedupe the controller's start requests, which fired three times per
download start because several upstream flows emit before isRunning flips.
---
